{"abstract":"Professor Joshua Brickman fra DanStem har i samarbejde med forskere fra The MRC Centre for Regenerative Medicine (CRM) ved University of Edinburgh identificeret en række faktorer, som regulerer embryonale stamcellers evne til at forny sig selv. Et af de centrale elementer er proteinet Oct4, og hvordan det får stamceller til at binde sig til hinanden. Den nye viden vil også gøre forskerne i stand til mere effektivt at omprogrammere voksne, somatiske celler tilbage til et stamcellelignende stadium. Sådanne celler benævnes også inducerede pluripotente stamceller eller iPS celler. iPS celler har mange af de samme egenskaber som embryonale stamceller; de kan i princippet dele sig i det uendelige, og de er ligesom embryonale stamceller pluripotente. Den markante forskel fra embryonale stamceller er, at iPS celler kan udvikles fra patientens eget væv. Resultaterne er publiceret i tidsskriftet Current Biology og kan på længere sigt få stor betydning for forskning i sygdomme som Diabetes og Parkinsons.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Keiding, Johanne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-393577"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Diabetes","Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences","Inducerede pluripotente stamceller","OCT4","parkinsons disease"],"level":"pop","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"derfor holder stamceller sammen","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.e-pages.dk/scanpub/410/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-393577","ids":["ku-00262de0-f16c-49bc-a73c-b16e814a4352"],"keyword":["Diabetes","Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences","OCT4","embryonale stamceller","inducerede pluripotente stamceller","omprogrammere","parkinsons disease"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D33CEC439555918043A725FD80C4D73C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.e-pages.dk/scanpub/410/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, The Danish Stem Cell Center, Secretariat"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Johanne","key":"keidingpau","last":"Keiding","locid":"28ede48e-469f-41de-9f7f-3dde7e1913b5","name":"Keiding, Johanne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09021787","09042369"],"issn_org":["09021787"],"issue":"6","newspaper":"Lægemagasinet","pages":"38-40","status":"p","title":"Lægemagasinet","title_org":"Laegemagasinet","volume":"27"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-00262de0-f16c-49bc-a73c-b16e814a4352"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Derfor holder stamceller sammen","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-393577","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
